  "notes": [
    "o→ue stem change in all present forms except *nosotros/nosotras* (dolemos)",
    "Past participle: *dolido*",
    "Like *gustar*, almost always used with **indirect object pronouns**: *me duele, te duele, le duele, nos duele, les duele*",
    "Singular subject = *duele*; plural subject = *duelen*: *Me duele la cabeza* — My head hurts; *Me duelen las piernas* — My legs ache",
    "*doler* can also be used figuratively: *Me duele que no hayas venido* — It hurts me that you didn't come",
    "Related: *el dolor* = pain; *doloroso/a* = painful"
  ],
